"aboutthewebsite": {
  "tags": [],
  "content": [
    { "content": "So... about this website... I made this ", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "more or less", "highlight": true },
    { "content": " from scratch. I just wanted to learn react (When I started wokring on this)  and now there's a bunch of handy stuff here that I made recently.. and a bunch of stuff that's years old but looked cool.", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "There's about (I think?) 13 different providers, a bunch of custom hooks etc. There's ", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "oodles", "highlight": true },
    { "content": " of junk too, it's not super well written. It fetches from the public folder in it's own repo... because github pages is ", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "a free host,", "highlight": true },
    { "content": "That's about it", "highlight": false },
    { "content": ".. Oh also, the custom format + rough editor for articles / posts is in here too under", "highlight": false },
    { "content": " /editor", "highlight": true },
    { "content": ".. Oh and what about generative AI use? ... well duh.. of course I used it. CSS is a pain in the butt afterall... ", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "dont use cursor / google antivgravity because it breaks everything", "highlight": true },
    { "content": " but I do use copilot & claude once im sure i understand something (or if im stuck, cmon, it's 2025 we're honest) ", "highlight": false },
    { "content": "Look, I used chatgpt to turn this string of text into a JSON object that has my highlight tags... like im not gonna sit here and do that manualyl when chatgpt is just there... provided it hasnt' added any random words or what not.... ", "highlight": true },
    {"content": "That said I used chatgpt extensively for my LaTeX stuff at uni and it insists on rewriting your words... Like, I just want you to fix my syntax not rewrite my nonsense into your nonsense", "highlight": false }
  ]
},



